# `git` (TASK-31 10h, ADR-0339, ADR-0347, ADR-0461; `make test-apps`, which turns @HOST@ and the TLS ports into
# values). git 2.56.1 as a POSIX program of the image, in its own directory /data/home/git (seen as ~/.config/git),
# with the repository of the current directory given by the shell, and its transport helper on libcurl and mbedTLS.
# The server is the host's `git http-backend` behind the test server's TLS listeners (tools/test-httpd): the valid
# certificate for test.zoraya, an expired one and one for another name. The disk's /system/tls/roots is the test PKI.
! panicked
! first process ended
! git tried to
! s3cret
! fatal: Invalid path
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
> git --version\r
< git version 2.56.1
< \r\n~>
# What the line gives git: its own directory, the toolchain set; no network, no repository yet.
> grants git status\r
< git gets (a POSIX program):
< its own files (it sees them as ~/.config/git)
< \r\n~>
# Who is committing: the global configuration, in git's own directory.
> git config --global user.name 'Ada Test'\r
< \r\n~>
> git config --global user.email ada@test\r
< \r\n~>
> cat /data/home/git/config\r
< name = Ada Test
< \r\n~>
# A new repository in a directory the line names: create-tree, and nothing else of the current directory.
> grants git init proj\r
< create proj, and change anything in it
< \r\n~>
> git init proj\r
< Initialized empty Git repository
< \r\n~>
> status\r
