< first notes
< \r\n~/proj>
> git --no-pager log --oneline\r
< first notes
< \r\n~/proj>
> git status\r
< nothing to commit, working tree clean
< \r\n~/proj>
# From a subdirectory the repository is the same one, and a ceiling the line writes is not the shell's (INV-0464-4).
> mkdir sub\r
< \r\n~/proj>
> cd sub\r
< \r\n~/proj/sub>
> git status\r
< nothing to commit
< \r\n~/proj/sub>
> GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=/home/proj git status\r
< nothing to commit
< \r\n~/proj/sub>
> cd ~\r
< \r\n~>
# Outside any repository: git says so, with no refused path (INV-0339-3).
> git status\r
< fatal: not a git repository
< \r\n~>
> git -C proj --no-pager log --oneline\r
< first notes
< \r\n~>
# Clone over https: the URL on the line is the host the command reaches, with the system's roots, and a name that is no
# public one needs the word (as for curl). The directory is the address's last part without `.git`.
> +net test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@ git clone https://test.zoraya:@TLSVALID@/git/repo.git\r
< Cloning into 'repo'
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< succeeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~>
> cat repo/README\r
< seed line
< \r\n~>
> cd repo\r
< \r\n~/repo>
> git --no-pager log --oneline\r
< the seed commit
< \r\n~/repo>
# A commit, and a push. With no word the host is not given (INV-0339-2): the helper has no connection and the server
